# Story 20: Stack Mode (Ctrl+S) (40s)
# Hook: Ctrl+S turns a stack into a flip-book -- rotate through your panes with j and k.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-020-stack-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Ctrl+S turns a stack into a flip-book -- rotate through your panes with j and k.

[00:04.0 --> 00:14.0]
Start rysh, then stack three panes with Ctrl+P, s -- twice over -- so the title reads one of three.

[00:14.0 --> 00:19.0]
Press Ctrl+S to enter stack mode. Now j and k rotate the deck.

[00:19.0 --> 00:26.0]
Press j to bring the next pane to the front. The counter ticks forward.

[00:26.0 --> 00:33.0]
Press k to rotate back the other way. You can fan through every pane in the group.

[00:33.0 --> 00:40.0]
Escape leaves stack mode. j and k -- that's all it takes to navigate a deck of stacked panes.

